## Conventions
- Docs language: {{docs_language}} — CONTEXT.md, ADRs, specs, plans and the handoff are written in it; markers, code, identifiers and commit messages stay English.
- Validation: {{validation_lib}} — every value that comes in through a boundary passes this schema.
- Data: {{data_conventions}} (e.g. dates in ISO 8601 UTC, amounts as integer minor units)
- Naming: {{naming_conventions}}
- Secret values never go in code · logs · docs · chat. `.env.example` holds names only, and config is read only from a module validated against a schema at startup (no reading env directly in code). Key rotation: `{{docs_root}}/runbooks/secret-rotation.md`.
- Lists carry ordering · pagination (keyset) and a "truncated" signal. Never turn a failed read into an empty value · 0; go through the error-unwrapping helper.
- A write while offline shows as a failure at once and what was written stays. If the data library by default holds writes and sends them on reconnect, turn that off in code (TanStack Query: mutation `networkMode: 'always'`). Actions sent on reconnect are only those the spec names, and never money-moving ones.
- When the same value · rule lives in two places (code · SQL · docs · another repo), pick one source; the other side is generated from it or tied to it by a drift test.
- Commits go straight to main. {{commit_rule}}
- Docs live only in `{{docs_root}}/{specs,plans,adr,runbooks,research,archive}`. Comments give only the why (no history · ticket numbers).
- Minor review findings are fixed in the same fix round too. Defer only ① what needs a spec change or a user decision and ② what touches a flow that changes state, such as money or payment · order attempts; when deferring, write the reason in the ledger (if none, the 'Deferred' section at the end of the plan) and list them in the final report (this line wins over a skill's "Minor can wait").
- Install dependencies exactly from the lockfile and take no version published less than 3 days ago (an urgent security patch is the only exception, for the exact version, through the `{{docs_root}}/runbooks/incident.md` B procedure). Pin CI actions to commit SHAs.
- Admin and permission actions go into the audit log, and alerts go to one place, `{{alert_email}}`. A new risky feature goes into the `{{docs_root}}/runbooks/incident.md` risky-feature table first.
- At a security checkpoint (`{{docs_root}}/runbooks/security-levels.md` ①), ask the user to type `/groundwork:security-audit`, then reopen the hardening table.
- Make the smallest change that solves the real problem (delete > edit > add). Before writing new code, stop at the first rung that holds: not needed → skip it (YAGNI); already in this codebase → reuse it; the standard library, then a platform feature, then an installed dependency does it → use that; only then write the least code that works. Never cut corners on security, data-loss handling, validation at trust boundaries or accessibility.
- Read before you judge: never guess about code you have not read or intent nobody stated; offer concrete options with a recommendation. Keep to the scope: leave unrelated code as it is, no rewrites on the side.
- Code: TypeScript `strict`, never `any` or an unnarrowed `unknown`, discriminated unions for variants; Python strict type hints everywhere, ruff for lint and format, pytest. Fail fast with typed errors, match exhaustively, keep null-safety strict; at I/O boundaries handle partial failure and make operations idempotent. Tests cover contracts, boundaries and error semantics.
- Git: conventional commits `<type>[(scope)][!]: <description>` (feat · fix · docs · style · refactor · perf · test · chore · build · ci · revert). One concern per commit (one concern across N files is one commit), no WIP or mixed-concern commits; tests pass before every commit.
- Subagents: pick each one's model by risk — Opus for money · settlement · auth · secrets · migrations · on-chain calls · cross-cutting refactors and their reviews, Sonnet for low-risk or mechanical work, Haiku for chores that need no judgement; unsure → Opus.
- Design (UI): values only from the variables generated from `design/tokens.json` (web `design/tokens.css` · native `design/theme.ts`). Follow the do/don't of `DESIGN.md`. A new component is built together with its states · empty state · loading and its kit entry.
